# Supabase for the app. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
# Both values are public by design: row level security is what protects data. Never put the
# database password or a secret key here.
#
# Local stack (`supabase start`, then `supabase status` shows both values):
#   - iOS simulator on this computer: http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   - Android emulator: http://10.0.2.2:54321 (127.0.0.1 there is the emulator itself), or run
#     `adb reverse tcp:54321 tcp:54321` and use http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   - A phone running Expo Go: this computer's LAN address, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:54321
#     (localhost on the phone is the phone itself). Plain http:// works in development builds
#     only; release builds require https://.
# Production: https://vhxcgmupopeochwvmwcv.supabase.co and the project's publishable key.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
